        "body": "## Why\n\n`scripts/cljk-mirror.cljk` in [network-awai/cloud-murakumo](https://github.com/network-awai/cloud-murakumo) (see network-awai/cloud-murakumo#254) mirrors every dependency to the extension it had before the `.cljk` rename so shadow-cljs can load it, and **refuses** when a `.cljk` file has no entry in the repo's `cljk-origin.edn`. This repo has 2 such files, which blocks building the murakumo.cloud Worker from `main` (`The required namespace ... is not available`).\n\n## What\n\nOnly `cljk-origin.edn` changes (appended); no source or behaviour changes.\n\n| file | recorded as |\n|---|---|\n| `src/kotoba/http/form_urlencoded.cljk` | `.cljc` |\n| `test/kotoba/http/form_urlencoded_test.cljk` | `.cljc` |\n\n## How the extensions were chosen\n\nFor files created after the rename there is no `.cljc`/`.cljs` ancestor in git, so the value follows the existing practice in these repos: `#?` present -> `.cljc`; a `scripts/` file or one that `require`s a `node:` module -> `.cljs`; `src/` using only `js/` -> `.cljc`; `test/` using only `js/` -> `.cljs`; no platform evidence -> `.cljc` (tests follow their subject). Checked against 106 already-recorded files that carry such evidence: 86 agree (81%); the rule above is the one refined from the 20 that did not.\n\n## Checked\n\n- `cljk-origin.edn` reads with `kbb` and has the appended entries; every tracked `*.cljk` in the repo is now registered with `.cljc`/`.cljs`/`.clj`.\n- Not yet verified end to end: cloud-murakumo consumes this repo at a pinned SHA, so the pin has to move to the merge commit before its build can drop `CLJK_MIRROR_GUESS`.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
